        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-12-28T20:45:23.159806Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Stepping gait that is multiped and involves a metachronal wave.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>metachronal stepping</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>multipedal walking</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>metachronal-stepping gait</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;Pseudopleuronectes americanus as well as others, in slow movement over the bottom undulate the marginal dorsal and anal with the tips of the rays in contact with the solid substratum thereby securing greater thrust.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
