        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Hippocampus hudsonius... when high speed, for a seahorse, is desired it leans forward with the vertebral column nearly horizontal and undulates the dorsal in localized anguilliform fashion.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000031"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The best examples of this characteristic are found among the African freshwater electric eels. The anal and caudal fins are missing, while the dorsal fin extends along most of the body length, tapering to a posterior point, and exhibits a large number of fin-rays (up to 200).&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1109/48.757275</dc:source>
