        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2009</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000161"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>subcritical jetting</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1988</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.137.1.421</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...subcritical... jet cycles...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000161"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>short-pulsed jetting</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2009</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...short pulsed and long pulsed jet...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000161"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;...brief squid Lolliguncula brevis...
The ratio of jet length based on the vorticity extent (Lω) to jet diameter based on peak vorticity locations (Dω) was &lt;3.0 for jet mode I...&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000161"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;In Nautilus the transition from jet mode 1 to jet mode 2 jets occurred at jet length to diameter ratio (Lj/Dj) of approximately 3 (jet mode 1 Lj/Dj &lt;2.16; jet mode 2 Lj/Dj &gt;3.16), similar to those observed in other jet propulsion swimmers (e.g. squid).&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1098/rsos.170467</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000161"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;With the lack of a consistent dependence of jet mode on speed, jet mode I and II do not fall within the purview of classical ‘gaits’ as defined by Alexander. Given the dual mode propulsive system of squids, both the jet and the fins need to be considered for proper identification of gaits (and probably a wider speed range).&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000162 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000162">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000160"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000498"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_quality"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-07-13T17:13:35.119922Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>pulsed jetting</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Jetting in which jet cycle period (contraction and refilling phase) increases with increased speed.

The ejected fluid develops into a leading vortex ring that separates or ‘pinches off’ from a long trailing jet.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>jet mode 2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>jet mode II</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>long jet</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>long jet pulse</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>escape jet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>starting jet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>supracritical jet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>supracritical speed jet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">long-pulsed jetting</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;...brief squid Lolliguncula brevis...
The ratio of jet length [based on the vorticity extent (Lω)] to jet diameter [based on peak vorticity locations (Dω)] was... &gt;3.0 for jet mode II...&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;In Nautilus the transition from jet mode 1 to jet mode 2 jets occurred at jet length to diameter ratio (Lj/Dj) of approximately 3 (jet mode 1 Lj/Dj &lt;2.16; jet mode 2 Lj/Dj &gt;3.16), similar to those observed in other jet propulsion swimmers (e.g. squid).&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;With the lack of a consistent dependence of jet mode on speed, jet mode I and II do not fall within the purview of classical ‘gaits’ as defined by Alexander. Given the dual mode propulsive system of squids, both the jet and the fins need to be considered for proper identification of gaits (and probably a wider speed range).&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000162"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>pulsed jetting</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2009</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000162"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Jetting in which jet cycle period (contraction and refilling phase) increases with increased speed.

The ejected fluid develops into a leading vortex ring that separates or ‘pinches off’ from a long trailing jet.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1242/jeb.027771</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Moreover, jet cycle period (contraction and refilling phase) decreased with increased speed for jet mode I (linear regression: d.f.=1, 28, F=36.365, P&lt;0.001, R2=0.547) but jet cycle period increased with increased speed for jet mode II (linear regression: d.f.=1, 27, F=8.562, P=0.007, R2=0.241).&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000162"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>jet mode 2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2018</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1098/rsos.170467</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
