        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Shifting toward lateral sequence from diagonal sequence supports the hypothesis that primates’ ability to transition between gait types (i.e., flexibility) may be crucial for successfully occupying their arboreal niches.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1002/ajp.23055</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
