        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Species that swim by passing waves of bending of the body from head to tail often switch from steady axial undulation to a saltatory &quot;burst-and-coast&quot; mode of propulsion at high speeds... Many percomorph fishes, as well as some less-derived actinopterygians, swim over low speeds by pectoral fin propulsion (termed labriform locomotion by Breder, 1926) and with increasing speed supplement paired fin movements with caudal fin oscillation.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1093/icb/36.6.555</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


