        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Studies of leaping and falling organisms tend to overemphasize arbitrary distinctions between gliding and parachuting to the detriment of the more critical issue of capacity for &apos;controlled descent.&apos;&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/j.1744-7429.2000.tb00506.x</dc:source>
