        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Trot gait that realizes a quadrupedal, suspended, walking pattern.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">walking trot</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">walking-trot gait</rdfs:label>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Reptiles and amphibians are historically thought to use “walking trots” at slow speeds (trots with a duty factor &gt;0.5) and “running trots” (trots with a duty factor &lt;0.5) at higher speeds.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
