        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Traversing-regime in which falling is initiated by releasing a support.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>drop</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">dropping</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>drop regime</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000193"/>
        <skos:example>&quot;For example, in the small tortoiseshell butterfly, Aglais urticae, males persistently court females, repeatedly tapping with their antennae until the female drops down into the vegetation, followed by the male who may then achieve a mating.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
