            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/posture"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-10-05T15:10:35.836844Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Posture that is on a relatively horizontal supporting stratum, body weight borne principally by the torso.

When an individual grasps a support, the extremity bears little more than its own weight. When lying on a side an individual may support the upper body with an elbow.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">lying</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>lying down</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reclining</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">lie posture</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;Liihrl (1956) said that Carrion Crows “often close their eyes with pleasure when they are lying in an ant hill.”</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Phycis regius has been observed to bury itself in sand and reclining on its side with the head protruding, watch the movements of other fishes with apparent interest.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Posture that is on a relatively horizontal supporting stratum, body weight borne principally by the torso.

When an individual grasps a support, the extremity bears little more than its own weight. When lying on a side an individual may support the upper body with an elbow.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1007/BF02381373</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;P13. Lie: Torso orthograde posture on a relatively horizontal supporting stratum, body weight borne principally by the torso. When an individual grasps a support, the extremity bears little more than its own weight. When lying on a side an individual may support the upper body with an elbow.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">lying</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1957</dc:date>
        <dc:source>https://digitalcommons.usf.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=5800&amp;context=wilson_bulletin</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
