    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000271"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000096"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000814"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/technical_realizing_routine"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-10-07T16:20:43.441417Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Technic which causes any structural modification of an object, so that it serves more effectively as a tool.

Modification means alteration of the dimensional physical characteristics of the tool, not simply its spatial orientation. There are four types of tool manufacture: detach, subtract, add/combine and reshape.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>manufacture</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">manufacturing</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>manufacture technic</rdfs:label>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;As ants work by inherited instincts and by inherited tools or weapons, and not by acquired knowledge and manufactured instruments, a perfect division of labour could be effected with them only by the workers being sterile;&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Technic which causes any structural modification of an object, so that it serves more effectively as a tool.

Modification means alteration of the dimensional physical characteristics of the tool, not simply its spatial orientation. There are four types of tool manufacture: detach, subtract, add/combine and reshape.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.4000/ejpap.2324</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Schumaker, Walkup and Beck define “tool manufacture” as “simply any structural modification of an object or an existing tool so that the object serves, or serves more effectively, as a tool.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>manufacture</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2008</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2007.09.028</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">manufacturing</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2008</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2007.09.028</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>manufacture technic</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;As ants work by inherited instincts and by inherited tools or weapons, and not by acquired knowledge and manufactured instruments, a perfect division of labour could be effected with them only by the workers being sterile;&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1859</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303</dc:source>
        <rdfs:comment>Darwin anticipated the concept of animal tool manufacture in negating it; however, our ontology tries to source the earliest positive label and synonym assertion dates, hence this quote is left here.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


