        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Exit in which an individual ends hibernation, before their dispersal.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>den emergence</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>den emergency</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>den exit</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">egress</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>egress exit</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;...C. horridus hibernacula and population... surveys should be conducted on
warmer days (daytime temperatures &gt;15–20°C) during the fall ingress and spring egress periods, when individuals congregate at or near hibernacula habitat...&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
