        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-10-13T13:28:33.989797Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Homeostasis that involves a reduced respiratory rate, and the reversible absence of feeding, movement, excretion, and breeding.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">quiescence</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>relaxing</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>rest</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>rest homeostasis</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;Carrion Crow...
in relaxed attitude, head tilted downward, tail drooped, and both wings hanging in front of, and well below, the perch.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Typical rest behavior in larval zebrafish includes floating with head down.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
