        <dc:source>doi:10.1146/annurev-neuro-071714-033857</dc:source>
        <rdfs:comment>No description in the source, but an illustration suggests encircling involves a stationary centre (e.g. a partner), whilst circling involves out of phase components (e.g. opponents circling each other head-tail).</rdfs:comment>
