        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Thalassoma cupido...
Spawning... mild chases contribute to the unstable nature of the aggregations.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jji1950/24/2/24_2_101/_article/-char/ja/</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000331"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;One possibility is that different stages of the behavior have a different organization. For example, animals might dynamically modulate their movements to adjust to the position of the prey during pursuit, but resort to more stereotyped motor patterns when consuming prey.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.cub.2019.11.022</dc:source>
