        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-10-21T19:07:16.164855Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Forage in which fruit is removed from vegetation.

This includes seed.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">harvesting</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>cropping</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">harvest forage</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;Chimpanzee...
Crop fruits in a tree, from shrubs on the ground...&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Fruit found in small trees was harvested most often by squatting, perhaps because the trunk itself was the largest and most stable perch from which to feed.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote>The term &apos;harvest&apos; is often used synonymously for different forms of farming and foraging, but is used selectively here.</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
