        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Relativity in which an animal unattaches another.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">dislodging</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>dislodging relativity</rdfs:label>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;In most species, females shake vigorously to dislodge the males and presumably the tight meshing of the male foreleg armature with the female wings help the males to remain mounted.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;In these organisms, terraces are functional in increasing friction between the exoskeleton and the substrate when a predator or a competitor tries to dislodge the crab from its shelter.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000394"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
