        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;In most species, females shake vigorously to dislodge the males and presumably the tight meshing of the male foreleg armature with the female wings help the males to remain mounted.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/j.1420-9101.2009.01826.x</dc:source>
