        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Perhaps one of the most notable derived antipredator adaptations in snakes is the rattle, an epidermal, soundproducing structure found on the tip of the tail in 29 species of rattlesnakes.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://search.proquest.com/openview/163eedf011944cd2321739b51d33470d/1?pq-origsite=gscholar&amp;cbl=18750&amp;diss=y</dc:source>
