        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The type of social organization (e.g., mating system and group size), however, can influence both the presence of social buffering and which conspecifics demonstrate the ability to buffer. Many species undergo seasonal shifts in social organization.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.3389/fetho.2023.1181774</dc:source>
