    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000449 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000449">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000472"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid3418"/>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_composite"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-11-17T11:36:14.405456Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Courtship in which a male remains close to a female for a prolonged period. 

This will usually be when she is receptive, in the context of sperm competition, and may involve fighting encroaching males.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">mate guarding</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>harem guarding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>post-copulatory mate guarding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>post-insemination mate guarding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>pre-copulatory mate guarding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>precopulatory guarding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>securing females</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>dominance</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>escorting</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>mate protection</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">mate-guarding courtship</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000385"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000829"/>
        <skos:example>&quot;In Metellina segmentata, males assess female quality (size and nearness to moult) before deciding on whether to guard or leave the female. In the congeneric M. mengei, the guarding male adjusts his fight tactics against intruders according to the reproductive value of the female, increasing fight intensity and duration with his mate’s body mass.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;In olive baboons, two lower ranking males sometimes form a team to gain access to estrous females. The troop’s dominant male usually escorts such females.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Male dik-diks are more territorial than their female counterparts: they engage in the majority of territorial scent marking and aggressively guard their mates during estrus.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Male western diamondback rattlesnakes (Crotalus atrox) have been observed mate-guarding females, which likely occurs in other rattlesnake species as well.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...harems are established and a rigid hierarchy is maintained based on the dominance of a single male over a group of females.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Yet, these single-species studies imply that the courtship in sepsid flies can be quite elaborate and may include male displays and precopulatory guarding.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3418">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000924"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000449"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3418"/>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1089/zeb.2012.0861</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...protecting resources (e.g., females)...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000449"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Courtship in which a male remains close to a female for a prolonged period. 

This will usually be when she is receptive, in the context of sperm competition, and may involve fighting encroaching males.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1007/s00265-014-1841-5</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
