        <rdfs:label>probing movement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;...parasitoid wasp species that... use their ovipositors to probe for prey...&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;First, some dolphins wear marine sponges to protect their rostrums while probing for food on the ocean floor; some mother dolphins demonstrate to their female young how to use the sponges.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Grammostola mollicoma (Ausserer, 1875) (Araneae, Theraphosidae)...
This could be due to the unusual high trajectory of the first pair of feet, probably used also as helper “probes” to detect obstacles.&quot;</skos:example>
