    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000288"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000289"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_realization"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-07-26T07:22:31.495774Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Relativity in which an organism disperses from its location with the aid of another organism by attaching to it.

This is regardless of whether the phoront actively searches for or more passively waits for the host.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>phoresis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>phoresy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>hyperphoresy</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">phoresy relativity</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;DISCOCEPHALI...
This placing of these fins appears to be associated with the ability of the fish to rotate on its longitudinal axis in swimming, apparently turning to any such position with ease. This is clearly necessary to insure attachment to sharks or other bodies. That fishes of such natatorial powers possess such a highly specialized organ as the cephalic disc is interesting, for they have apparently suffered no particular degeneration of their power to care for themselves in a locomotor sense, for of course they must first catch their shark.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Fossilized accounts of phoresy include mites, springtails, and pseudoscorpions, with some records of mites dating back 85 million years, and pseudoscorpion records dating back 40 million years.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Madeira, again, is inhabited by a wonderful number of peculiar land-shells, whereas not one species of sea-shell is confined to its shores: now, though we do not know how seashells are dispersed, yet we can see that their eggs or larvæ, perhaps attached to seaweed or floating timber, or to the feet of wading-birds, might be transported far more easily than land-shells, across three or four hundred miles of open sea.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Relativity in which an organism disperses from its location with the aid of another organism by attaching to it.

This is regardless of whether the phoront actively searches for or more passively waits for the host.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1111/brv.12654</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;We believe these definitions are complementary, and that phoresy can be defined most broadly as the behaviour of one organism (the phoront) to disperse from one location to another with the aid of another organism (the dispersal host) by attaching to that organism, regardless of whether the phoront actively searches for or more passively waits for the host.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>phoresis</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2021</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/brv.12654</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>phoresy</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2021</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/brv.12654</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>hyperphoresy</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2021</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/brv.12654</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">phoresy relativity</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;DISCOCEPHALI...
This placing of these fins appears to be associated with the ability of the fish to rotate on its longitudinal axis in swimming, apparently turning to any such position with ease. This is clearly necessary to insure attachment to sharks or other bodies. That fishes of such natatorial powers possess such a highly specialized organ as the cephalic disc is interesting, for they have apparently suffered no particular degeneration of their power to care for themselves in a locomotor sense, for of course they must first catch their shark.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Fossilized accounts of phoresy include mites, springtails, and pseudoscorpions, with some records of mites dating back 85 million years, and pseudoscorpion records dating back 40 million years.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/brv.12654</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000498"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Madeira, again, is inhabited by a wonderful number of peculiar land-shells, whereas not one species of sea-shell is confined to its shores: now, though we do not know how seashells are dispersed, yet we can see that their eggs or larvæ, perhaps attached to seaweed or floating timber, or to the feet of wading-birds, might be transported far more easily than land-shells, across three or four hundred miles of open sea.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000334"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2024-12-23T21:12:51.454852Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Assessment which assumes moral possession.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ownership</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>owning</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>possession</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reserving</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>There are probably more appropriate ways to conceive of behaviour that looks like &apos;ownership&apos;, such as &apos;control of access&apos;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>ownership assessment</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000291"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000378"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000382"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000449"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000834"/>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Assessment which assumes moral possession.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;EVANS (1935, 1936) found that in Anolis carolinensis the heaviest male usually won the fight. If, however, the lighter male was already in possession of the territory, then the bigger one was often defeated. KRAMER (1937) found the moral effect of the possession of a territory in the lizard Lacerta melisellensis.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ownership</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1967</dc:date>
        <dc:source>https://open.uct.ac.za/handle/11427/13101</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>owning</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>possession</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>reserving</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>There are probably more appropriate ways to conceive of behaviour that looks like &apos;ownership&apos;, such as &apos;control of access&apos;.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2019.12.009</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...conceiving of ownership is unfeasible in animal societies...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000499"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ownership assessment</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


