    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000643"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ZFA_0005389"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_entity"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-07-26T08:49:13.357966Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Streamlining which results from Injection of high momentum fluid into the boundary layer from the gills.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>boundary layer fluid injection</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>developed jets</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Whilst prescient, Breder&apos;s insight about active (pulsed) fluid injection does not appear to be effective in practice amongst fishes, although a passive relation to it does in the form of continuous ram with the gill slits left open.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">induction streamlining</rdfs:label>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Returning to the fishes, it should now be obvious that the water ejected through the gill clefts of typical acanthopterygians is extremely similar in its effect to that of this new mechanical device that has actually propelled a model successfully. It seems, however, almost impossible to obtain an accurate measure of just what locomotor advantage this exhalation of water may be to most species, but it is readily demonstrated to be a real item in others.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Streamlining which results from Injection of high momentum fluid into the boundary layer from the gills.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>https://www-dr.wcupa.edu/sciences-mathematics/biology/fFish/documents/1998ImaginativeDragReduction.pdf</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Injection of high momentum fluid into the boundary layer has the capacity to delay both transition and separation. The effluent from the gills of fish could potentially introduce kinetic energy into the boundary layer.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>boundary layer fluid injection</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1998</dc:date>
        <dc:source>https://www-dr.wcupa.edu/sciences-mathematics/biology/fFish/documents/1998ImaginativeDragReduction.pdf</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Injection of high momentum fluid into the boundary layer...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>developed jets</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1926</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Whilst prescient, Breder&apos;s insight about active (pulsed) fluid injection does not appear to be effective in practice amongst fishes, although a passive relation to it does in the form of continuous ram with the gill slits left open.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://www-dr.wcupa.edu/sciences-mathematics/biology/fFish/documents/1998ImaginativeDragReduction.pdf</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Flow visualization in fish, however, has shown the pulsed flow during active respiration increases turbulence. The location of the gill slits anterior of the maximum thickness of fish (i.e,, position of lowest pressure) would enhance respiratory flow rather than surface flow. During passive or ram ventilation in scombrid fish, the mouth and gill coverings are kept open so that water can continuously flow over the gills without pumping. The constant swimming motion of the fish maintains the flow. Ram ventilation does not prevent turbulence, but it appears to extend the laminar region of the boundary layer by 13-100%.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">induction streamlining</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1926</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;induced streamline system&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000501"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Returning to the fishes, it should now be obvious that the water ejected through the gill clefts of typical acanthopterygians is extremely similar in its effect to that of this new mechanical device that has actually propelled a model successfully. It seems, however, almost impossible to obtain an accurate measure of just what locomotor advantage this exhalation of water may be to most species, but it is readily demonstrated to be a real item in others.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000083"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002415"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/sub_activity_by_entity"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2026-07-26T12:37:10.634945Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Splaying that spreads the tail.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>tail spreading</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>caudal fin spreading</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tail splaying</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Splaying that spreads the tail.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;These muscles spread the tail fin, and the inner branch can also bend the tail sideways.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>tail spreading</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...spread the tail fin...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>caudal fin spreading</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...caudal fin is always spread and closed as a whole.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">tail splaying</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000503 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000503">
