        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;When C. elegans animals are removed from food, they display a stereotyped sequence of two consecutive locomotion states. For the first 15 min, they engage in a local search state (also called “area-restricted search”) consisting of a high frequency of high-angle turns and omega bends.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1534/genetics.120.303539</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


