While thus fixing on the worm the fish forms a slight Sickle-shape, and then strikes forward grasping the free tip of the worm. Hence this maneuver is the same as that used in capturing free-swimming prey, except it has a different orientation.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>http://www.nativefishlab.net/library/textpdf/15582.pdf</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
