        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Both the male and female Gryllus bimaculatus used in this study were sexually mature virgins of similar age... the mate guarding intensity (the number of body judders and antennal whips/rotations) was recorded every minute until the male entered into courtship (determined by production of long courtship song whilst backing towards the female;&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1007/s10164-009-0176-6</dc:source>
