    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000541"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000438"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-01-21T15:20:25.440084Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Switch that is part of a highly predictable, rigid pattern of serially and spatially configured activity modules.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>fixed motor pattern</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">stereotyped pattern of behavior</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>stereotypy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>fixed action pattern (FAP)</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>modal action pattern (MAP)</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>automatic</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>fixed</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>inflexible</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>rigid</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ritual</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>The literature mixes up use of certain terms for &apos;normal&apos; and &apos;abnormal&apos; behaviours: in this case we use the term &apos;stereotyped&apos; to refer to &apos;normal&apos;, if invariant, behaviour, and not to &apos;abnormal&apos; behaviour such as maladaptive perseveration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>stereotype switch</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;...the flock of teal may release sham attacks by the falcon, resulting in the isolation of a member of the flock. The final stoop, capture, kill, plucking, and eating form a relatively simple and stereotyped&quot; chain of consummatory acts.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;The rarer jaw movement was highly stereotyped, comprising a rapid, large-amplitude depression of the jaw concurrent with cranial elevation. This movement was exclusively associated with capture events and was preceded by an attack swim or S-strike, or occurred in isolation as a ‘‘suction’’ capture. Thus, different capture strategies in zebrafish larvae emerge by combining different stereotyped tail kinematics with stereotyped jaw kinematics.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...stereotyped, inflexible tooling, which can be identified by the use of “a single tool for a single purpose in a particular context”, typically in species showing only one type of tooling.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Switch that is part of a highly predictable, rigid pattern of serially and spatially configured activity modules.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.beproc.2014.10.001</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>fixed motor pattern</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">stereotyped pattern of behavior</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1966</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.2307/4083155</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>stereotypy</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1966</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.2307/4083155</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>fixed action pattern (FAP)</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1961</dc:date>
        <dc:source>http://www.nativefishlab.net/library/textpdf/15582.pdf</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>modal action pattern (MAP)</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2015</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.beproc.2014.10.001</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>automatic</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>fixed</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1965</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853965x00138</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>inflexible</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2021</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/tops.12554</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>rigid</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1965</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853965x00138</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ritual</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1965</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853965x00138</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The literature mixes up use of certain terms for &apos;normal&apos; and &apos;abnormal&apos; behaviours: in this case we use the term &apos;stereotyped&apos; to refer to &apos;normal&apos;, if invariant, behaviour, and not to &apos;abnormal&apos; behaviour such as maladaptive perseveration.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/eff.12212</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...abnormal behaviours, such as stereotypic behaviour, inappropriate time budgeting or the occurrence of atypical behaviour....&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;...the flock of teal may release sham attacks by the falcon, resulting in the isolation of a member of the flock. The final stoop, capture, kill, plucking, and eating form a relatively simple and stereotyped&quot; chain of consummatory acts.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.2307/4083155</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The rarer jaw movement was highly stereotyped, comprising a rapid, large-amplitude depression of the jaw concurrent with cranial elevation. This movement was exclusively associated with capture events and was preceded by an attack swim or S-strike, or occurred in isolation as a ‘‘suction’’ capture. Thus, different capture strategies in zebrafish larvae emerge by combining different stereotyped tail kinematics with stereotyped jaw kinematics.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.cub.2019.11.022</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000540"/>
