        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;It is possible to demonstrate the conflict between fleeing, backward or forward, and suppression of movement in a Badis badis by placing it in a small aquarium with inadequate shelter. Tapping on the glass with one&apos;s finger, varying the strength and distance of the tapping, causes the fish to lie still, suddenly jump forward and immediately back, and so forth. Thus the behavior switches back and forth rapidly between the possible outlets of Fright.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
