                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000543"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_06105011"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/locomotion_realizing_regime"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-02-06T12:36:13.506217Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Swimming-regime that maintains some tilt in mid-water.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">drifting</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>vertical drift</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>coasting</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>floating</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>hanging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>drift regime</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;...the juvenile labrid Novaculichthys taeniouru, which looks like drifting algae (the deception enhanced by its seemingly disoriented movement);&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Nocomis leptocephalus...
As the male’s body relaxed parallel to the current, he drifted down stream to resume interim behavior (e.g., pit-posturing). Once released, the female continued to rise vertically into the water column, then quickly rolled upright and... drifted to a position behind the male from where she might initiate another spawning sequence.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;The drifting back is generally not done in a position with the body axis parallel to the current, but at an angle to it equal to... the best possible position to initiate motion against the stream flow, instead of having to make that first flexure from the less effectual position directly in line with the flow.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Swimming-regime that maintains some tilt in mid-water.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1089/zeb.2012.0861</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">drifting</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1926</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/p.203769</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
