        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;...the juvenile labrid Novaculichthys taeniouru, which looks like drifting algae (the deception enhanced by its seemingly disoriented movement);&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://zoolstud.sinica.edu.tw/Journals/44.3/299.pdf</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000574"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Nocomis leptocephalus...
As the male’s body relaxed parallel to the current, he drifted down stream to resume interim behavior (e.g., pit-posturing). Once released, the female continued to rise vertically into the water column, then quickly rolled upright and... drifted to a position behind the male from where she might initiate another spawning sequence.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2</dc:source>
