        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-02-06T21:50:43.456088Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Transition that involves an animal&apos;s heading vector.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>orientating</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">orienting</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>reorienting</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Be careful not to confuse this with placement (e.g. the orientation of the thumb to the palm of the hand) or postural changes (e.g. inclination of the body to the ground, such as when lying or standing).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>orienting transition</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000523"/>
        <skos:example>&quot;Female crickets orienting to a male calling song pause frequently and change direction primarily during pauses.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Macaca radiata...
To begin a descent, the monkeys first reoriented themselves to align the liftoff and target lateral stems with the transverse plane of the body.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
