        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The assumptions of the model were explicitly based on marine cleaning mutualism involving the cleaner wrasse Labroides dimidiatus (the service provider), which feeds on the ectoparasites of other reef fishes (the clients).&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1093/beheco/aru194</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000611"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Two Whistling Ducks may be preening normally side by side when one will approach the other and either begin nibbling the other&apos;s head or present its own head to be nibbled. In the posture of presentation, the eyes are partly or completely closed and the head is stretched out toward the other bird and held rigid in one position.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853965x00138</dc:source>
