        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The benthic longhorn sculpin demonstrates different use of dorsal and ventral fin regions during both station holding and swimming behaviors. During station holding, the ventral pectoral fin rays are splayed and contact the bottom surface of the tank, anterior to the dorsal region of the fin, and are believed to be to be gripping the bottom.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
