        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Fruit found in small trees was harvested most often by squatting, perhaps because the trunk itself was the largest and most stable perch from which to feed.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1002/ajpa.1330870108</dc:source>
