        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000715"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;It is easy to imagine how water captured with krill could be extruded from the mouth through the spaces between the cusps on Lobodon&apos;s teeth. Juvenile crabeater seals feeding on fish in captivity sucked them in individually and ejected excess water from the sides of their mouths.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>ISBN:9780226315737</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000715"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Next to moving their tails up and down, the expelling of water from their mouths by rorqual whales is the most massive, single action taken by any organism that has ever lived.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>ISBN:9780226315737</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000715"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Thalassoma cupido...
...pair dash rapidly upward, usually about 25-50 cm, where the eggs and milt are released.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/jji1950/24/2/24_2_101/_article/-char/ja/</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000715"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Bodily secretions include saliva, wax, silk and even excrement, all of which can serve as effective glue for cementing external materials together.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1016/j.cub.2021.09.082</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000715"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;In Cryptobranchus and Andrias, males guard oviposition sites in burrows or under rocks. Females are attracted to these sites and lay large yolky eggs in long strands, as in the anuran genus Bufo. Strands may be extruded from one oviduct or from both oviducts simultaneously. The resident male moves over the strands as they are laid and extrudes white, ropy masses of sperm, fertilizing the eggs.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>ISBN:9781482294347</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000082"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002497"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/movement"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-05-25T13:52:03.467358Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Movement that involves extensive lateral excursions of an extremity.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>lateral swinging</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>sweep</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">sweeping</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>sweeping movement</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;As the tail sweeps back and forth, it creates a series of alternating vortices. Each stroke of the fin creates a single donut-shaped vortex that is linked to the vortices of previous strokes. Each vortex represents the momentum imparted to the water by the fish&apos;s body and tail.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;The work of construction seems to be a sort of balance struck between many bees, all instinctively standing at the same relative distance from each other, all trying to sweep equal spheres, and then building up, or leaving ungnawed, the planes of intersection between these spheres.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Movement that involves extensive lateral excursions of an extremity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.00424</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>lateral swinging</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.00424</dc:source>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2003</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>sweep</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">2000</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1126/science.288.5463.100</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">sweeping</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303</dc:source>
        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1859</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>sweeping movement</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;As the tail sweeps back and forth, it creates a series of alternating vortices. Each stroke of the fin creates a single donut-shaped vortex that is linked to the vortices of previous strokes. Each vortex represents the momentum imparted to the water by the fish&apos;s body and tail.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1126/science.288.5463.100</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000716"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The work of construction seems to be a sort of balance struck between many bees, all instinctively standing at the same relative distance from each other, all trying to sweep equal spheres, and then building up, or leaving ungnawed, the planes of intersection between these spheres.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.5962/bhl.title.82303</dc:source>
