        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;...a wild Mallard reacts to an alarming stimulus by suddenly raising its head to assume a very erect posture. This reaction of alarm functions as an important signal transmitting fleeing mood within a group of birds.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853965x00138</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


