        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Tilapia natalensis...
The eggs of the fishes of the Tilapia-type are snapped up immediately after they have been spawned... As long as she is carrying eggs the female makes only weak respiratory movements in which the mouth is only slightly opened. These movements having lasted for about one minute, the female makes more intensive chewing movements for about half a minute. In each of these movements the mouth is opened wider than usually and shut completely afterwards; the bottom of the mouth is moved up and down and when the mouth is open the eggs can be seen rolling about in it.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
