        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000893"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;The stimulating effect of the courting activities does not always seem to shorten the time till spawning. This we observed a few times in pairs of Astronotus ocellatus and C. bimaculatum, of which the male was more energetic than the female. As soon as the female carried out some feeble quivering or nipping-off movements on the substrate, the male rushed on and began to perform the same movements so vigorously that the female was pushed aside and had to leave the stone. Undoubtedly this tended to retard spawning in the female.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
