        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;A. ibis...
For these few days before pairing, each male occupies a small territory in the colony, displaying on it and vigorously defending against intruders an area of two or three metres radius. It is usual for this territory to be abandoned and another nest used for nesting after a mate has been acquired.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
