    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000118"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000317"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-10-26T15:58:12.843325Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>calling movement</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Ethotype in which an adult draws in endangered young to itself as their protective cover.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym xml:lang="en">young-calling</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>leading the young</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">young-calling ethotype</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000906"/>
        <skos:example>&quot;Tilapia natalensis...
In case of some danger the female, after having made some violent movements against an eventual intruder... retreats towards the young and assumes a diagonal position, the longitudinal axis making an angle of about 10 or 20 [degrees] with the horizontal, the head lower than the tail. In this position she swims slowly backwards... the young move... closely along the body towards the mouth in which they actively penetrate or are passively taken up by the female.&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>calling movement</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ethotype in which an adult draws in endangered young to itself as their protective cover.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">young-calling</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Calling the young;&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>leading the young</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1950</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">young-calling ethotype</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000909"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Tilapia natalensis...
In case of some danger the female, after having made some violent movements against an eventual intruder... retreats towards the young and assumes a diagonal position, the longitudinal axis making an angle of about 10 or 20 [degrees] with the horizontal, the head lower than the tail. In this position she swims slowly backwards... the young move... closely along the body towards the mouth in which they actively penetrate or are passively taken up by the female.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1163/156853981X00220</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000591"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid6836"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000167"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/context_by_entity"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-11-06T17:54:41.77654Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Piping in which the trunk rests on the substratum while, with a buccal bubble present, the head is held at the water surface.

The head may be either neutral or positively buoyant.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>buccal bubble hydrostasis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>bubble releasing</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">bubble-gulping</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>bubble-holding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bubble piping</rdfs:label>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;All bubble-gulping species possessed a negatively buoyant trunk, regardless of the presence of a swimbladder... lift derived from the swimbladder and the bubble act independently when the fish is performing ASR in the arched position. The bubble-gulping species P. olorum and Chlamydogobius, both of which lack a swimbladder, performed ASR (arched position) in a similar manner to those bubblegulping  species with a swimbladder. The non-bubble-gulping species F. tamarensis performed ASR when arched but used the beached position most frequently. All of the bubble-gulping species appeared to use bubble lift combined with the flexibility of the body to arch the head upwards, placing the mouth at the water surface. As a result, we considered lift and weight acting on the head to be independent from lift and weight acting on the trunk.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;Two obvious roles for the buccal bubble are to enhance ASR by further oxygenating the water prior to ventilating the gills and to provide O2 directly to respiratory tissues in the buccal cavity, as occurs in some gobies.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6836">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000668"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6836"/>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Piping in which the trunk rests on the substratum while, with a buccal bubble present, the head is held at the water surface.

The head may be either neutral or positively buoyant.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;These data show that during ASR with a buccal bubble present the trunk rests on the substratum while the head is either neutral or positively buoyant and held at the water surface.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>buccal bubble hydrostasis</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1995</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...hydrostatic role for the buccal bubble.&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>bubble releasing</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1995</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;...release their bubble...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">bubble-gulping</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1995</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>bubble-holding</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">1995</dc:date>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">bubble piping</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;All bubble-gulping species possessed a negatively buoyant trunk, regardless of the presence of a swimbladder... lift derived from the swimbladder and the bubble act independently when the fish is performing ASR in the arched position. The bubble-gulping species P. olorum and Chlamydogobius, both of which lack a swimbladder, performed ASR (arched position) in a similar manner to those bubblegulping  species with a swimbladder. The non-bubble-gulping species F. tamarensis performed ASR when arched but used the beached position most frequently. All of the bubble-gulping species appeared to use bubble lift combined with the flexibility of the body to arch the head upwards, placing the mouth at the water surface. As a result, we considered lift and weight acting on the head to be independent from lift and weight acting on the trunk.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000910"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Two obvious roles for the buccal bubble are to enhance ASR by further oxygenating the water prior to ventilating the gills and to provide O2 directly to respiratory tissues in the buccal cavity, as occurs in some gobies.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1242/jeb.198.1.79</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000911 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000911">
