        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Parotia carolae...
Court clearing. — A male nondisplay court-preparation behavior. A range of activities in which leaves, leaf litter, or other forest debris are removed from the court floor.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1093/auk/123.4.967</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000913 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000913">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000272"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000727"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_00010483"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <terms:conformsTo rdf:resource="https://github.com/Active-Animals/Ontology/patterns/technical_by_kinetics"/>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>Ditch Townsend</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2025-11-07T10:56:42.23654Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Construction that covers a space with a collection from the surrounding substrate.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>depositing</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>piling</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>burying</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>filling</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>masoning</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>mound-building</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym xml:lang="en">mounding</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>plating</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>walling</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>covering</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>nest-building</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>piling construction</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;Megapodes construct nest mounds from which the young emerge fully independent of adults, and these birds select mound sites with thick vegetative cover to prevent desiccation of the incubating eggs.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;Nocomis Girard is a genus of nest-building chubs (Cyprinidae)...
...the male excavates a concavity which he fills with pebbles to form a platform...&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:example>&quot;The cutlips minnow collects around 300 identical pebbles and builds a mound 35 cm wide and 10 cm high, and tilefish make coral mounds up to 1 m high.&quot;</skos:example>
        <skos:scopeNote>&quot;At the most ‘basic’ level, nest-building efforts may culminate in a seemingly haphazard arrangement of piledup materials, such that a mound or plate (located on or above the ground, respectively) of sticks and twigs provides birds with a nesting substrate...&quot;</skos:scopeNote>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000913"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDefinition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Construction that covers a space with a collection from the surrounding substrate.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:contributor>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4277-2151</dc:contributor>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1674/0003-0031(2000)144[0187:SBITBC]2.0.CO;2</dc:source>
        <rdfs:comment>Termite and similar mounds are excluded, because they are structures which emerge from other constructing activities such as cementing. Our meaning predominantly involves the use of loose material.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ACTAN_0000913"/>
