        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;Apterygote insects transfer sperm indirectly via spermatophores or sperm drops. Spermatophores are usually deposited on the ground or on special silk threads. They are then picked up by the female, sometimes with active male participation and close physical contact between male and female, sometimes in dissociation.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1111/j.1469-185X.2007.00029.x</dc:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
