        <owl:annotatedTarget>&quot;‘Following and scavenging’ associations are by far the most common type of attendant associations.

‘Interspecific joint hunting’ occurs when two species of active predators hunt together.

‘Hunting by riding’ occurs when a predatory associate swims alongside or above a nuclear species that is either non-predatory or feeds on different prey.

...‘aggressive mimicry’ occurs when the associate species is a predator, and it mimics the nuclear species, that is harmless.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
