        <oboInOwl:hasDefinition>Adduction that results from anal fin abducting.</oboInOwl:hasDefinition>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">anal-fin abduction</rdfs:label>
        <skos:example>&quot;The shrimpfish (Aeoliscus punctulatus) maintains a vertical orientation with the head
pointed downward... The median fins (dorsal, caudal, anal) are positioned along the venter of the body and are beat or used as a passive rudder...&quot;</skos:example>
    </owl:Class>
