The height of the upward dash varies considerably, from a minimum of approximately 13 cm to a maximum of about 1.5 m. Immediately after spawning, the fish move slightly apart and swim downwards with great rapidity. The wrasses may reassemble upon returning to the bottom or they may disperse. The entire spawning sequence occurs within the span of about one second.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
