Aerial reproductive swarming of this magnitude also serves as predator defense, as the massive pulse of food for local predators overwhelms the predator community to the point of satiation.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:source>doi:10.1007/978-3-319-68576-2_3</dc:source>
